          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy a mower built for mulching: a dedicated mulching deck like Toro's Recycler, or twin and stacked blades like Toro's Atomic system and EGO's Select Cut. The Toro Recycler Max is our overall pick, the EGO LM2156SP is the one to buy for battery power, and the Craftsman M310 is the budget option if you mow often.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then give it what it needs. Follow the one-third rule, mow when the grass is dry, keep the blade sharp and the deck clean, and mulch autumn leaves weekly. Do those things and almost any decent mower will mulch well; skip them and even the best will leave clumps.
